1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[Queen] Your first mission

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
will be to lead all the soldiers
here to capture my food.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
I want you to capture

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
more of those highly
nutritious organisms for me.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,000
[Colt] I shall.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
[opening theme music playing]

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
[singer singing in English]

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
[singer singing in English]

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
[singer singing in English]

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

14
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
VERY X RAPID X REPRODUCTION

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
[narrator]
The Chimera Ants are insatiable carnivores

16
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
which are currently under the designated
quarantine level one.

17
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Once these creatures have evolved
beyond two meters in length,

18
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
humans no longer stand a chance.

19
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[farmer sighs]

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Huh?

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Huh.

22
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
[insects buzzing]

23
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Hey, what the hell is that?

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[farmer] Huh?

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
[farmers exclaim frightfully]

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[Colt]
Target the fully grown ones!

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
They will provide the most nutrition.
Now go!

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
[farmer screams]

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
[grunts]

30
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
[all screaming]

31
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[men screaming]

32
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
[shuddering]

33
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[grunts]

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
[gasps]

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
[Kite] A Chimera Ant Queen
stays on the move

36
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
until she finds a site she likes.

37
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
During her search,
she'll produce more and more soldier Ants,

38
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
building her own personal army.

39
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Once she's chosen a location,

40
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
she produces a swarm of construction Ants

41
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
to build her castle with incredible speed.

42
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
She will remain within
that fortress until her death.

43
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Should a queen who has
reached two meters in height

44
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
develop a taste for human flesh,
no one is safe.

45
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Entire towns and villages will go missing,

46
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
victims of the queen's limitless hunger.

47
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Nothing so far.

48
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
I just finished checking out
the past six months,

49
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
and the largest group I could find
only numbered ten.

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Hey, can we try looking
for missing people individually?

51
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Don't be ridiculous.

52
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
You know how many
hundreds of thousands of people

53
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
go missing worldwide each year?

54
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
[Killua] We could still see which areas
have the highest concentrations, though.

55
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Mmm, well… no good.

56
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
This data is two years old.

57
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
[Gon] Maybe we should start
by checking for sightings.

58
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
[Killua] Yeah,
seeing a two-meter-tall insect

59
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
would be a big deal.

60
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
[Spinner] Sure, that goes without saying,
but we tried that already.

61
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
We didn't turn up anything.

62
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
We might be getting
all worked up over nothing, guys.

63
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Maybe so.

64
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Bring up all the tidal data
from the day the arm was found.

65
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[Spinner] It was discovered
right around here.

66
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Now try going back to ten days ago.

67
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[keyboard clacking]

68
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Locate any currents that could
potentially have carried the arm

69
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
to that location in that period of time.

70
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Wait. What do you mean?

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
I mean that we should consider
the possibility the arm was severed

72
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
after the Chimera Ant
washed up somewhere else.

73
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
I see.

74
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Seems it could have come
from any of the Balsa Islands.

75
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:09,000
And unfortunately
that includes the Mitene Union.

76
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Seriously?

77
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Oh! Where the NGL Autonomous Region is.

78
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Yes, and that's
not to mention East Gorteau.

79
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
No chance of getting information
out of those two countries.

80
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
What's the NGL?

81
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,000
NGL's an acronym
that stands for Neo-Green Life.

82
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
[Stick] It's a country founded by people
who reject modern technology,

83
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
choosing instead to live in nature.

84
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
[Spinner] Here it is.

85
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[Spinner]
They primarily communicate by mail,

86
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
and primary travel is by horseback.

87
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Anyone who brings technology
into the country could be executed.

88
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Like back in '87, there was
a three-man television crew

89
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
that was caught trying
to enter the country

90
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
in order to get a story.

91
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
One was executed,
and two are still jailed.

92
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:59,000
99% of its 2.17 million population
belong to the NGL Party.

93
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
The rest are volunteers.

94
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[Kite] Let's assume for now
that the Chimera Ant washed ashore there.

95
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
How would the NGL's citizenry react?

96
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
I doubt they'd do anything.

97
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
When a deadly epidemic
spread through the area,

98
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
they refused international medical aid,

99
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,000
because they preferred to let nature
run its grisly course instead.

100
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Even if they tried to contact
the outside world,

101
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,000
it would be too late
by the time word arrived.

102
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
So if the arm
that was discovered did belong

103
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
to the Chimera Ant Queen,
then it's entirely possible

104
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,000
that she's already begun
constructing her nest.

105
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[Colt] A contest?

106
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[Alligator Ant]
Yeah, between you and me.

107
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Just a friendly challenge
to see which one of us

108
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
can bring the Queen more humans to devour.

109
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
-What do you say, huh?
-[scoffs]

110
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Hmm? You're running away?

111
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Accept my challenge!

112
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[Colt] What?

113
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Are you ordering me around?

114
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Tell me. Why should I follow
an order from you?

115
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:08,000
I only follow orders given to me
by the Queen herself.

116
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Oh, give me a break.

117
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
You're just scared of losing.

118
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
See, my squad is comprised
of elite soldiers.

119
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
I can beat any squad
in this entire castle.

120
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Hey, I know.

121
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
I should get the other
squad leaders in on this,

122
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
make it a group thing.

123
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
If we all compete against each other,

124
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
we're bound to capture more prey.

125
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
So that's the goal?

126
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
I see. I agree with your premise.

127
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
If we gather more prey,

128
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
the Queen will be quite pleased indeed.

129
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Well, okay, then. That settles it.

130
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
However, the quality of the prey
matters as well.

131
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
It's very important to ensure

132
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,000
that the Queen eats
only highly nutritious humans.

133
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
That guy's such a stiff,
it's not even funny.

134
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
But that's what makes him so endearing.

135
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
He's as loyal
as he is dedicated to the cause.

136
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
I presume that the human

137
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
from which he was created
was also quite earnest.

138
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
[crying]

139
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Oh.

140
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Where are you going?

141
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
I told you to get some rest, didn't I?

142
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
I'll go bring her back.

143
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Don't bother. It won't help.

144
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
But she's been going to the forest
every single morning

145
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
and spending her whole day searching.

146
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
That's right.

147
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
She'll probably collapse
from exhaustion soon.

148
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
But she still can't stop
looking for her missing children.

149
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
That's what it means to be a parent.

150
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[farmer 1] How long has it been now?

151
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
How many days ago
did Kurt and Reina vanish?

152
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
[farmer 2] It's like the spirits
whisked them away.

153
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
-[children laughing]
-[boy] Yeah!

154
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Huh?

155
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Wow. Those bugs are big.

156
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Huh?

157
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[Colt] It's an area we haven't raided yet.

158
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
-[girl screams]
-[gasps]

159
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
[grunts]

160
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
[gasps]

161
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
[sobs]

162
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
[man screams]

163
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Mommy!

164
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[farmer 1] It was them,
those awful monsters!

165
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
They must have been the ones
that stole your children from you!

166
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[gasps]

167
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[elder grunts]

168
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[crowd murmuring]

169
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Excellent. The Queen will be most pleased.

170
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
This will be more than sufficient,
I'm sure.

171
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
-[gunfire]
-[gasps]

172
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[hostages screaming]

173
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
[gasps] What?

174
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Exterminate the insects quickly.

175
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
That's Gyro's direct order.

176
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Gyro? What is Gyro?

177
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
The name of our king, you fool!

178
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Damn it.

179
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
[Spinner] Okay, I just bought us
tickets to the Mitene Union.

180
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
But in order for us to reach the NGL,

181
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
it looks like we'll
have to take an airship

182
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
to the neighboring Rokario Republic,

183
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
and then we can travel by land
the rest of the way.

184
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Well, those nasty rumors
"ants" gonna help.

185
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Just kidding. [laughs]

186
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Nasty rumors?

187
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Like what?

188
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Have you heard of DD?

189
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
[Gon] Uh, no.

190
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
[Kite] It's a drug propagating rapidly
in urban areas worldwide.

191
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
It's derived from the Bira Tree,

192
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
which is native to the Mitene Union.

193
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
And not only are they
native to the region,

194
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
but they claim over 80%
of the world's Bira Trees

195
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
are located in the NGL.

196
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Okay, so the nasty rumors are

197
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,000
that the NGL is manufacturing it?

198
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
They're still only rumors.

199
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
No one has been able
to prove it publicly yet.

200
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
The country is locked down tight.

201
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
When anybody tries
to get in and investigate,

202
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
they're instantly executed.

203
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
They are?

204
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
[Pokkle] He wasn't killed?

205
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
-Hmm?
-No.

206
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
If he had been captured trying to uncover

207
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
the NGL's secrets,
then there's a good chance

208
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
he would have been executed
like that TV crew man.

209
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
But this reporter wore a recording device.

210
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Our goal was to intercept
the final message,

211
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
and that's how we did it.
When the message was played…

212
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:38,000
[reporter] M-Monsters! Gigantic bugs!

213
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
[static crackling]

214
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Gigantic bugs, huh?

215
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Mmm. So what do you think?

216
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Hmm. I can't be sure
without knowing a lot more.

217
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
-[chuckles]
-[men] Huh?

218
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
I'll have to see for myself.

219
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
I mean, I am the only
Magical-Beast Hunter here.

220
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
That settles it.

221
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
I'll go get three tickets for the journey.

222
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
-[Ponzu] Make it four.
-[men] Huh?

223
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
[Pokkle] Ponzu?

224
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
I'm coming with you guys.

225
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
You can't! This is too dangerous!

226
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
You don't even have
a professional license yet,

227
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
and we're talking about
the NGL here, remember?

228
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
And that's why.

229
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
You're not allowed to bring technology

230
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
into the NGL, right,
so if they catch you

231
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
with any cell phones
or wireless communicators,

232
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
guaranteed you'll be
arrested on the spot.

233
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:28,000
All I'm saying is if there's any trouble,
you guys'll need me,

234
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
or rather, you'll need them.

235
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[buzzing]

236
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:40,000
If you have a letter for someone,
they can carry it anywhere you like.

237
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
[chuckles]

238
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
I get it.

239
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
They'll sure come in handy.

240
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
[indistinct announcements]

241
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:02,000
It may be too late to ask this,
but are you sure you want to come along?

242
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Of course.

243
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
You weren't kidding
about the "late" part, huh?

244
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
As you know, we have no idea
what the situation is inside the NGL.

245
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,000
There may very well be
a swarm of giant Chimera Ants

246
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
already hunting humans down.

247
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
And if that does indeed
turn out to be the case,

248
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
then my priority will be saving them.

249
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
So, be aware that I may
not be able to help you two.

250
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:31,000
If you're going to join us,
you must be able to protect yourselves.

251
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Right. I got it.

252
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
We're okay.

253
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
And if it happens to be me

254
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
who finds himself in danger,
then leave me there.

255
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Uh…

256
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
You got it?

257
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[tense music playing]

258
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[Alligator Ant] Hey,
that's a pretty good haul.

259
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Well, it's less than half
of what my squadron delivered,

260
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
but it's okay.

261
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[Colt] My focus was quality,
and I wasn't competing with you.

262
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[scoffs] Whatever.

263
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
So anyway, did you hear?

264
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
That turtle guy's group ran into
a bit of human resistance.

265
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
You don't say.

266
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
[page turns]

267
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Hmm. What you saw
were probably things called guns.

268
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Guns?

269
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
To put it simply, it's a barrel

270
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
that launches small
metal projectiles, or bullets,

271
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
using the explosive force of gunpowder.

272
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,000
It's one of the most commonly
used human weapons.

273
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
I have no idea what you're talking about.

274
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,000
If you want to know more,
then read these books.

275
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,000
They're wonderful and filled
with quite useful information,

276
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:57,000
such as how humans think, behave,
and function as a society.

277
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[Turtle Ant] Maybe you can answer
a question for me, then.

278
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
These humans, do they have armies, too?

279
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Why do you ask?

280
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Well, because what attacked us out there

281
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
was an army.

282
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
That much I know.

283
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
They belong to a military body

284
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:15,000
led by an authoritative figure,
much like us.

285
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Oh, yes, and I have another question.

286
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
They mentioned something about a name?

287
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
A name? Hmm.

288
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
I can see why you're confused.

289
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:31,000
It's a human idea and one that
we do not make use of ourselves.

290
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:34,000
In terms you would understand…

291
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
It seems humans are capable
of more than we thought.

292
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
I was beginning to think
all they could do was cry and run away.

293
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
And why does that surprise you?

294
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
You and I are quite different
ourselves, are we not?

295
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
It's only natural that humans would have
unique traits as well.

296
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Their blood, after all,
flows through all of our veins.

297
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
[tone ringing]

298
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
[Queen] Squadron leaders, assemble!

299
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Squadron leaders, assemble!

300
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
The Queen is summoning us.

301
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
[Queen] Squadron leaders, assemble!

302
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Do you get a headache

303
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
every time the Queen calls to us,
or am I the only one?

304
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
No, my ears start ringing like crazy
whenever I hear it.

305
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
A shame, really.

306
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
If only the Queen could talk like we do.

307
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
[Queen] I shall now begin preparation
for the birth of the King.

308
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Every day from this day forward,
you will deliver me 50 humans.

309
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[Chimera Ants] Yes, Majesty!

310
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
[Turtle Ant] Your Majesty,
may I ask a question?

311
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
[Queen] Yes. Speak.

312
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Among the humans
are soldiers like ourselves, my Queen,

313
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
with weapons to use against us.

314
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:08,000
If I may make a suggestion,
we must fortify our defenses

315
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
in preparation for a potential attack.

316
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
We have already come up
with a few options.

317
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Would you care to hear them?

318
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
[Queen] I will allow you
to decide your own course.

319
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:23,000
For now, I must focus entirely on my son.

320
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
[Turtle Ant gasps]
Thank you, Your Majesty.

321
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:31,000
But one more thing,
may we have your permission to have names?

322
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[Queen] And what is a name?

323
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
[Turtle Ant] It's like a label, my queen,

324
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:39,000
one that can be used to identify
each of us individually.

325
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[Queen] Fine. Do as you please.

326
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[Turtle Ant] I am eternally grateful.

327
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
[Queen] Curious creatures.

328
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:55,000
They're assertive and desire things
called names to be distinct.

329
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
They place a high value on individualism,

330
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:02,000
yet strive with one another
for the good of the colony.

331
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:11,000
I suppose I'm just as peculiar
to find this change fascinating.

332
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Perhaps, just perhaps,

333
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:17,000
I, too, have faint traces
of human blood within me.

334
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Regardless, I cannot help
but feel great anticipation.

335
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Yes. I can sense you already,

336
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,000
almost as if recalling
a memory from my own past.

337
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
I promise you this,

338
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:39,000
you shall stand at the pinnacle
of all species!

339
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Names, amusing little things.

340
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
The three elite royal guards,

341
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I shall come up
with a name for you myself.

342
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
[airship whirring]

343
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[Killua] Well,
what did you just decide?

344
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[Gon] You remember
what Kite said before we left,

345
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
that we should escape
without him if he's in danger?

346
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,000
[Killua] Yeah. He didn't make it
sound like it was a choice.

347
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,000
[Gon] Right.

348
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,000
And that's why neither one of us
felt comfortable saying anything.

349
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,000
But there's something
that I've been thinking about.

350
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Do you really think Kite,
a guy Ging respects,

351
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
can ever actually be in that much danger?

352
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
You said before that Ging had a reason
for bringing Kite and me together.

353
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
So do you still think that?

354
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Yeah.

355
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Lately I've started
to think you're right.

356
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
I don't know the reason,
and maybe I never will,

357
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
but I can't give up.

358
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
And it doesn't matter
what's going on here.

359
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:52,000
I just don't want
to disappoint Ging, you know?

360
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Or me. I couldn't forgive myself, either.

361
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
I won't run away.
That's what I've decided.

362
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Damn it.

363
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
You had such a serious look on your face,

364
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
I was expecting something big,

365
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
but it's the same stuff as usual.

366
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
[Gon] Huh? I thought about it a lot.

367
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
I even ran a bunch
of simulations in my head.

368
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
[Killua] Think all you want,
you're still Gon.

369
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
If someone said you should abandon them,

370
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:23,000
there's no way you'd ever do it.

371
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
[Gon sighs]

372
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
You make it sound like I
wasted my time considering it.

373
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Okay, then, so what about you?

374
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
Don't know.

375
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
I guess I'd just think about it
when the time comes.

376
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Hold on. You mean you might run away?

377
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Depends on what happens.

378
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Look, I don't really do
these hypotheticals.

379
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,000
[Gon] Fine, but what if--

380
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,000
[Killua] Look, I already told you.

381
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,000
I don't know what I'd do, okay?

382
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
I never decide 'til it's time.

383
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
[narrator] And so, the airship,

384
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
along with the group
and all of its other passengers,

385
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
begins the journey
for the Mitene Union

386
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
still completely unaware

387
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:06,000
of the cruel fate
which lies in store for them.

388
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[closing theme music playing]

389
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:22,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

390
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:32,000
[epic music playing]

391
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
[Gon] Next time, "No good NGL."

392
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Killua] Ready, go!

393
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:39,000
[Gon] It's probably not
in this coun… [sighs]

394
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[Killua] And there's your outtake, folks.

395
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
